.TH man 1 "31 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME 
	mkmv - mkdir then mv things there
.SH SYNOPSIS
	mkmv source[s] destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	makes the destination directory. then moves the files there. if dest already exists it's just mv.
.SH OPTIONS
	mv default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose\n\n
	mkdir default options do not work because mkdir only uses the last argument
.SH EXAMPLES
	mkmv *.csv csvs
	mkmv sdifji.py ../../ijsdif
.SH BUGS
	probably none
